cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Plugsight, please cite it as below."
title: Plugsight
abstract: "Plugsight is a macOS-native, agent-first USB security monitor. It detects and explains what plugs into your Mac: it scores devices, scans mounted storage, and writes a plain-language timeline. It is a detector, not a blocker; local-first, MCP-native, and MIT-licensed."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "plugsightlabs"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/plugsightlabs/plugsight"
url: "https://plugsight.com"
keywords:
  - usb-security
  - macos
  - mcp
  - agent
  - endpoint-security
  - local-first
  - badusb
